{
  "vcon": "0.4.0",
  "uuid": "6899e5b2-6f83-8552-80dc-a2476d51a7c8",
  "created_at": "2026-01-12T19:01:20-05:00",
  "subject": "Inbound call, Public Works",
  "parties": [
    {
      "name": "Nadia Okafor",
      "role": "resident",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    },
    {
      "name": "Lorraine Medeiros",
      "role": "clerk",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    }
  ],
  "dialog": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-12T18:49:20-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Public Works storm line, this is Lorraine."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-12T18:49:26-05:00",
      "duration": 21,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Hi, yes, good evening. I know it's after hours, I saw the message on the main number that said to try this line for storm things. Is this the right one?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-12T18:49:47-05:00",
      "duration": 16,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "It is. City Hall is closed for the day, but this line is open for storm cleanup calls. What can I help you with?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-12T18:50:03-05:00",
      "duration": 20,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay. There's a tree down. Well, it's my mother's tree. Well, it was her tree, it's still her tree, it's just on the ground now. Sorry. It's across her driveway."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-12T18:50:23-05:00",
      "duration": 13,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "No problem. A tree across the driveway. Is it the whole driveway, or can a car get around it?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-12T18:50:36-05:00",
      "duration": 23,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Nothing gets out. She's in her eighties, she doesn't drive much anyway, but I can't get my car in either. It came down in the wind. The coastal storm, the one that ended Saturday."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-12T18:50:59-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay, the storm that wrapped up Saturday. And what's the address?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-12T18:51:07-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "165 Dixon Street. In the North End."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-12T18:51:12-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "165 Dixon Street, North End. Got it. And your name?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-12T18:51:19-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Nadia Okafor. O-K-A-F-O-R."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-12T18:51:22-05:00",
      "duration": 13,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okafor, thank you. Nadia, is the tree on your mother's property, or is it out by the street?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-12T18:51:35-05:00",
      "duration": 26,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Um, it's in her yard. Near the front. The trunk is by the corner of the yard and the top of it is across the driveway. Actually, hold on, sorry, I'm in a shop and the door keeps going."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-12T18:52:01-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "That's all right. I can hear the bell."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-12T18:52:07-05:00",
      "duration": 36,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yeah, it rings every time someone comes in. I'm picking up a few things and I wanted to call before you closed out. Anyway. The main thing I want to know is who I'm supposed to call for this. Is it the city, or is it on us, or is it the electric company?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-12T18:52:43-05:00",
      "duration": 42,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Good question. In general, a tree that's on private property is the property owner's to deal with, so that would be your mother's responsibility to have it cut and removed. If it's in the street or on the city's right of way, that's the city. And if it's touching or hanging on a power line, that's the utility, and you shouldn't go near it."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-12T18:53:25-05:00",
      "duration": 15,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "It's not on a line. I don't think. There's a wire that goes to the house, though. Is that a power line?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-12T18:53:40-05:00",
      "duration": 13,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "It could be. Can you see whether the branches are resting on that wire, or pulling it down?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-12T18:53:53-05:00",
      "duration": 19,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I was there around four. It looked like the branches were next to it, not on it. But it was getting dark, so I couldn't swear to it."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-12T18:54:12-05:00",
      "duration": 31,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay. Then I'd say, treat it as if it might be live. Keep your mother and anybody else away from that part of the driveway. If you see the wire sagging, sparking, or down, call the electric company right away, and call 911 if anyone's in danger."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-12T18:54:43-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Right. Okay. I'll tell her not to go out front."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-12T18:54:50-05:00",
      "duration": 21,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Good. Now, if the wire's fine and it's just the tree, then it's on your mother's side. Does she have a tree service she's used before, or someone you could call?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-12T18:55:11-05:00",
      "duration": 17,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "No, my brother always handled that, he's, um, no, he's not around here. Sorry, that's not what you asked. No, we don't have a service."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-12T18:55:28-05:00",
      "duration": 24,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "That's fine. I can't recommend a particular company, but there are several local tree services, and after a storm they're usually busy, so it may take a few days. Calling a couple for quotes is normal."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-12T18:55:52-05:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay. And the city doesn't come take it away if it's in the yard?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-12T18:56:02-05:00",
      "duration": 23,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Not from private property, no. The city crews focus on trees in the roadway and on city land. If any part of it were hanging into Dixon Street itself, that we'd want to know about."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-12T18:56:25-05:00",
      "duration": 21,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "It's not in the street. The driveway goes in from the street and the tree is over the driveway. The end of it might touch the sidewalk. Is the sidewalk the city's?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-12T18:56:46-05:00",
      "duration": 23,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "The sidewalk is generally in the public right of way, so if limbs are blocking the sidewalk, that's something we can look at. Let me put that in. Is it blocking people from walking past?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-12T18:57:09-05:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "A little. You'd have to step into the grass. Maybe a branch or two."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-12T18:57:19-05:00",
      "duration": 19,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay. I'll note a report for 165 Dixon Street, tree down on private property, branches partly over the sidewalk, possible wire near the house. Does that sound right?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-12T18:57:38-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes. That's right. Though I'd say the wire thing is a maybe."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-12T18:57:47-05:00",
      "duration": 13,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "A maybe on the wire, understood. I'll write it that way. Will you be the contact, or your mother?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-12T18:58:00-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Me. Please call me, not her. She doesn't hear well on the phone."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-12T18:58:09-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Sure. What's the best number?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-12T18:58:13-05:00",
      "duration": 2,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "401-555-0173."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-12T18:58:15-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "401-555-0173. Nadia Okafor. And that's a cell?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-12T18:58:20-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes, cell. I'll have it with me."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-12T18:58:25-05:00",
      "duration": 20,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Good. Someone from public works may call to check on the sidewalk part. They probably won't be out tonight, and tomorrow depends on how many calls are ahead of yours."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-12T18:58:45-05:00",
      "duration": 14,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "That's fine. Is there anything we're allowed to do ourselves in the meantime? Like, can I cut some of it?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-12T18:58:59-05:00",
      "duration": 29,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "If it's clear of any wires and you're comfortable and have the right equipment, small limbs, sure. But a trunk that size, under tension, across a driveway, I'd leave to a professional. Trees that have come down can shift when you cut them."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-12T18:59:28-05:00",
      "duration": 12,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yeah. No, I wasn't going to do the trunk. I have a hand saw. That's about it."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-12T18:59:40-05:00",
      "duration": 11,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "A hand saw is fine for light branches. Just stay well away from that wire."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-12T18:59:51-05:00",
      "duration": 13,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay. And for the future, if there's another one, the number I call is this one? For a tree?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-12T19:00:04-05:00",
      "duration": 24,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "During the day you'd call the Public Works office. For storms and evenings, like tonight, this line is the one. If it's an emergency, like a tree on a house or on a wire, use 911."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-12T19:00:28-05:00",
      "duration": 24,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay. Good. That's what I needed. Let me just make sure, so I have it right. Tree on her property is hers to deal with. In the road, the city. On a wire, the electric company."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-12T19:00:52-05:00",
      "duration": 12,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "That's exactly it. And the sidewalk branches, I've put in for the city to take a look."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-12T19:01:04-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Great. Thank you, Lorraine."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-12T19:01:08-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "You're welcome, Nadia. I hope you get your driveway cleared soon. Take care."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-12T19:01:17-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "You too. Bye."
    }
  ],
